  "notes": "No Limit's dark mode, and the only entry in this batch whose distinctives are all *subtractions*. ⛔ **The slowest tempo on the axis (78–92, centre 84)** and natural minor throughout, moving in 4-bar blocks — `i–VI–VII` or `i–iv`. ⛔ **\"Fewer rolls than the party-side records\"** is the sourced claim, so `hihat.rolls.freqPerBar` sits at 0.10 — the floor of this batch's authoring band and the lowest of the fifteen — and `snareRoll.gapProb` at 0.65 is the highest, which is the same statement said twice: when a roll does happen here it is full of holes. ⛔ **Sparse 8th hats**, not the parent's stop-start triplet grid and not No Limit's 16ths: `hihat.base` is `8th` with `fillDensity` 0.45, thin enough to hear the pads and still thick enough that every seed gets hats. ⛔ **Minor 9th pads** — `extensions.ninth` at 0.22 is the highest in this batch by a factor of two, `voicing.style` is `open` and its register drops to 45 so the pad sits under the vocal rather than over it. ⛔ **\"Long sustained sub ... low register emphasis\"**, so `bassline.rhythm` is `mirror_kick` at `followRootsProb` 0.86 over a kick that plays three or four times a bar — two or three low roots per bar, which reads as sustained at 84 BPM — and the 808's own register is the lowest here at 19–31. `reese_sustain` was not used: it emits one note per chord and saturates. ⚠ **The pad-only outro** the research names is `sectionRules.outro` cut to `chords` with `decay: true`, which no other entry in this batch does. ⛔ **Confidence is `low`, and that is the research's verdict** — \"medium-low — label bench and era sourced; parameters inferred\" — with the 78–92 band marked **[LOW-CONF]** as well. Inferred: the key list, every velocity and register bound, `intervals`/`contour`, the perc lanes, `offSnare.prob` and the chord-duration spread. ⚠ `snareRoll.pitchWalk` is inherited. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
